  "brief_markdown": "This mock study illustrates a CityLab research result for 12 fictional Houston apartment communities. The property identifiers, rents, aerial measurements and statistics are synthetic and are not observed CoStar or Vexcel results. The example question compares green cover with maximum monthly asking rent while controlling for community units, construction year and categorical building class.\n\nThe illustrative adjusted association is $18 per month for each additional percentage point of green cover, with a 95% interval from -$4.10 to $40.10 and a p-value of 0.09. These numbers were chosen to demonstrate the response format; no regression was fitted. The interval crosses zero, so even this illustrative output would not justify a clear positive finding.\n\nA real study would review the measurement area, imagery dates, rent pricing bases and control completeness before interpreting the result. The interface should let reviewers inspect synthetic detections and propose corrections, while future handlers refresh the statistics and brief. Twelve communities are a small observational sample, and this example provides no causal conclusion or investment recommendation.",
